  "conversionNotes": [
    "Costs are printed in Warp Tokens; recorded as gc-equivalent numbers.",
    "Scanned PDF with overlaid artwork: the Plague Monks Ld looks like 6 in the page image (partly obscured), and Plague Monk cost reads 45. Please verify.",
    "Monk Initiates are listed under Heroes (0-2) at 20 warp tokens, with an equipment list shared with other heroes. Max 2 each for Plague Monks and Monk Initiates.",
    "Rat Ogre and Giant Rats are listed under Henchmen (groups of 1-5); Rat Ogre has max 1 (0-1).",
    "Dice conversions: Disease Dagger 'natural 6 on a hit roll' -> natural 12; 'armour save of 6+ if none' -> natural 12 save; Toughness test 'Roll a D6, higher than Toughness' -> roll a D12 (Toughness is doubled by the app); Censer 'a result of 6 always inflicts a wound' -> natural 12. Please confirm the intended Toughness-test handling.",
    "The Clan Pestilens special skills (Black Hunger, Censer Bearer, Rotten Body, Contagious, Ignore Pain) and the special rare equipment (Warpstone Amulet, Fog-enhancing shards, Liber Bubonicus, Liturgicus Infecticus, Scroll of the Rat Familiar, Clan Pestilens Banner) are not transcribed. Plague Priest could learn Horned Rat magic via Liber Bubonicus plus Magical Aptitude.",
    "Special skill column is recorded as 'Special' (Clan Pestilens special skills).",
    "Maximum profile for Clan Pestilens Skaven (M5 WS6 BS6 S4 T5 W3 I7 A4 Ld7) is not part of the schema and was left out."
  ]
